  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ORDA Harvest Plus 2013-15(17) - ORDA Next Phase</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ORDA Harvest Plus 2013-15(17)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Goal (Impact): To contribute for achieving improved food and nutrition security at household level.
Purpose (Outcome): Sustainably improved productivity and income of 9,600 smallholders (7941 Male and 1659 FHH) and 1860 women and youth by 50% through effective and gender equitable productive resources utilization by the end of the project period.
Applicable top level indicators:
By the end of the project average productivity of selected high value crops(Teff, Maize, Mung-Bean, Carrot and Onion) increased from 12.7 to 19 qt/hao Field crops: 10.68 to 16 qt/hao Vegetables: 92.66 to 139 qt/ha
By the end of the project average annual income of target households increased from 7,746 to 11,620 ETB.o Smallholders: from 9,437 to 13,401 ETB.o Women and youth: 3,238 to 6,867 ETB.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objectives: Approx.  2150 smallholder irrigators will produce and supply high value crops to the market 2) Increasing households income s 3)  Improve household gender relation 4 Based on HARVEST improve    ORDA&apos;s ability to serve the poor in rural Amhara</narrative>
